# Git must not rewrite the contents of this repository on checkout.
#
# The conformance corpus is byte-exact test vectors. An `OMSTR`'s content is
# significant whitespace, so a fixture whose line endings git translates is a
# fixture that tests something *different* on Windows — which is not
# hypothetical: the first Windows CI run decoded `standard/omstr-whitespace` as
# "  two  spaces\r\n" against an expectation of "  two  spaces\n", and reported
# every source file as unformatted because JuliaFormatter saw CRLF.
#
# So: text files are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree on every
# platform, and the corpus is exempt from translation altogether.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact test data: never translated, never diffed as text.
test/corpus/** -text
*.bin -text -diff
